import Mathlib

/-!
# Logarithmic prismatic cohomology: target signatures

**This file is not the roadmap and is not exhaustive.** The definitive specification is
`README.md`; references of the form §8.n are to its subsections.

None of the headline theorems of Layer 8 can be stated against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti.
Mathlib supplies Witt vectors, monoid perfections, divided powers, schemes, sheaves and derived
categories, but the logarithmic and prismatic objects needed for these statements are absent.
The following signatures are therefore deferred:

* §8.0: the algebraic Witt–Frobenius Riemann–Hilbert equivalence and extension by zero need
  algebraic Frobenius modules and their derived solution functor on the étale site.
* §8.17: the equivalence between perfect log prisms and perfectoid log rings needs both
  categories, including their log structures and Frobenius.
* §§8.28–8.29: log Hodge–Tate comparison and completed base change need log formal schemes,
  log differentials, log prisms and log prismatic cohomology.
* §§8.35–8.42: log crystalline, q-crystalline and q-de Rham comparisons, semistable AΩ
  comparison and the C_st diagram need the log crystalline and q-crystalline complexes,
  their sites and the semistable AΩ complex.
* §§8.47–8.57: derived log Hodge–Tate comparison, descent, Nygaard graded pieces and
  completeness, de Rham comparison and the Frobenius isogeny need animated prelog rings,
  the Gabber log cotangent complex, derived log prismatic cohomology and its filtrations.
* §8.58: Breuil–Kisin descent and perfectness need the Breuil–Kisin log prismatic complex.
* §§8.61–8.69: the scheme/adic/diamond and prismatic Kummer-étale comparisons need log
  adic spaces, log diamonds and their Kummer-étale and quasi-pro-Kummer-étale sites.
* §§8.71–8.75: the p-Kummer criteria, corrected Laurent equivalence and proper smooth
  saturated pushforward need Kummer local systems, their p-Kummer subcategory and Laurent
  F-crystals on the absolute saturated log prismatic site.
* §§8.76–8.79: the A_inf étale comparison, log PD Frobenius rigidity, Hyodo–Kato scalar
  comparison, BKF theorem and semistable-chart comparisons need the log cohomology complexes,
  the augmented log PD deformation base, A_crys and Breuil–Kisin–Fargues modules.

These objects require the constructions specified in the README, rather than a few auxiliary
definitions on the supplied carriers. No headline statement is replaced by an abstract
cohomology parameter or an unspecified predicate.
-/

